     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the FDA-labeled maximum for metformin, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. At that dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially. It's also unusual for a single dose to be 1700 mg, since the usual maximum per dose is 850 to 1000 mg.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals.** That's 2,550 mg/day, the max for IR.\n- **1000 mg twice daily with meals.** That's 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg three times daily with meals**, or another dose.\n- **1700 mg total per day**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n\nIf 1700 mg three times daily is what you intended, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
